WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.535
-Hi everyone, welcome to
the "Tonight Show."

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.403
I'm Jimmy Fallon.
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.706
I threw my -- I threw my voice
out yesterday.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:10.677
-You did?
-Doing the guy with the mask --

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.346
The guy with -- the man mask.
-Oh, right, right.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:16.082
-I threw it out.
So I'm a little raspy.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.417
There's a little extra bonus
tonight.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.652
I got a little raspy voice.
-Raspy.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.487
-It's mysterious.
-Worth it.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.357
-Mysterious, you don't know
if I'm -- if this is a bit

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.692
or if this is real, you know.
I kind of like it.

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.061
I kind of might
want to keep it.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.962
I'm talking to a couple
vocal coaches.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.465
[ Light laughter ]
To see if I can keep it.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:33.633
-Make it a thing?

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.868
-Yeah, I'm gonna make it
my thing.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.502
-Make it a thing?
-Yeah, this is gonna be a thing.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.704
It started off, you know,
lemonade out of lemons.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:40.740
-I don't think -- I don't think
it's a good fit.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.442
[ Light laughter ]
-It's --

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:44.076
What are you talking about?
This fits me.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:46.445
-Um, I don't know.
-You know what, do you remember

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.781
when we were on the
Thanksgiving Day float?

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.650
No, not that story.
-Oh, okay.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.652
-The other story. No, no.
-Okay.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.153
-No, no, not --
No, not Richard Simmons.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.321
That was great.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.789
But, no, this is when
we were on the float

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.491
and I was up -- I forget
what we were on,

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.627
some giant something,
and I was screaming,

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:02.862
I was so excited.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.230
It was the first time.
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.498
-I was like,
"Happy Thanksgiving!

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.766
Happy Thanksgiving!"

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.634
Yelling, and you go,
"Dude, dude.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:12.705
Save your instrument."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.574
-Yeah, you lost your voice
like blocks into,

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:18.444
like, an 80-block parade.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.845
-I was so excited, man.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.314
I was like, I've never
been on a float.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.182
I was yelling at everybody.
Yelling back, "I love you too!

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:25.951
Happy Thanksgiving!"
And then, yeah, I lost it.

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:27.420
Save your instrument.
-Yeah, man.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.255
-Wow, I even wrote that
in my diary.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.524
-[ Laughs ]
-Anyways, we're back, everybody.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.493
And thanks so much again
for watching last night.

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:37.564
This is episode two
of the in-studio shows,

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:40.667
and it -- it feels good be --
to be back here.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.402
So, let's get to some jokes.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.471
Well, guys, as cases of
coronavirus continue to surge

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:48.174
across the country, President
Trump has made a decision

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.243
regarding next month's
Republican National Convention.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:53.779 line:0%
-The Republican National
Convention, which is set

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:56.783 line:0%
to take place in Jacksonville
six weeks from now,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.153 line:0%
we're told now by Republicans
familiar with the planning,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:03.489 line:0%
a lot of that may be
moving outdoors.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.558
-Yeah the president is now
holding a three-day

00:02:06.558 --> 00:02:10.263
outdoor event in Florida
in August.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.031
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.166
It will be worth watching just
to see Trump lap up

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.835
glasses of water like
a thirsty Golden Retriever.

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:17.837
[ Slurps ]

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.639
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.607
And poor Mike Pence
is going to be sweating

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:25.044
like he's sitting through
a "Drag Race" marathon.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.846
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.882
Yeah, Trump decided to move
the convention outside

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.252
after meeting with his
most trusted advisors,

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.454
Chuck Woolery
and the My Pillow guy.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.288
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.791
Well, guys, as you probably
heard, the Trump family

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.727
has been in a legal battle
with the president's niece

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:44.397
for weeks now over the release
of her tell-all book.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.832
Let's see how that turned out.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.067 line:0%
-An explosive new tell-all
about the Trump family

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.535 line:0%
hits shelves today.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:52.405 line:0%
On the eve of its release,
a judge lifted a gag order

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:56.342 line:0%
on Mary Trump, allowing her to
speak freely about the book.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.777
-Trump lost his lawsuit
against John Bolton

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:00.813
and his book became
a bestseller.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.548
He lost his lawsuit
against his niece

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.717
and her book is on its way
to becoming a bestseller.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.120
Mr. President, I'm personally
asking you,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.588
please sue my new
children's book.

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.390
[ Laughter ]
Thank you.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.426
Trump's niece actually wrote
a pretty interesting book.

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:16.729
Chapter 11 is all about
his family businesses.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.465
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.000
That's right. Yeah.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.535
Thank you. Thank you.
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.170
I owe you one.
I owe you one.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.105
That's right, there's a new
tell-all book,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.873
and there's a lot of
pretty big claims.

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:30.543
One of them is that Trump
regifted a basket of food

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.745
to his niece for Christmas.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:36.382
Regifted.
And the caviar was missing.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.717
Here to talk about it is the
one guy who changed his mind

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:40.519
on Trump because of this.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:43.122 line:0%
-Well, hey there, Jimmy.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.991 line:0%
-Thank you so much for being
here, sir.

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.827
So I hear that you've been
a die-hard Trump supporter

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:51.497
for years, and after this
gift basket thing,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.333
you had a change of heart?
-Well, that's right.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:57.537
Before, when I thought about
Trump, I was like, yes!

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.671
But now after this
gift basket thing,

00:03:59.671 --> 00:04:02.408
I'm like, oh, unh-unh!

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.309
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:04.309 --> 00:04:06.512
-Really? Really? This?

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.514
-I know a bombshell
when I hear one, Jimmy.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.650
And Caviar Gate, I mean,
just slap me on the ass

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.852
and rewrite the history books.
Whoo!

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.021
I mean, party foul.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:18.291
When it comes to gifts, baskets,
and fish eggs,

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.192
I want to be on
the right side of history.

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:22.895
-Well, now look, I got to say
I'm surprised that this

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.897
tipped it over for you.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:27.500
What about the other stuff
Trump has been accused of,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.336
Russian meddling
or ignoring coronavirus,

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.971
lying about crowd sizes,
tear-gassing protestors

00:04:32.971 --> 00:04:34.941
for a photo op?

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.777
-That's really just the
president being the president,

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:41.047
but this caviar thing --
I mean, total monster,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.983
it's almost like, I can't
believe I'm saying this,

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:47.286
it's like he doesn't care
about other people.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.188
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:52.257
Either regift the whole basket
or don't regift it at all!

00:04:52.257 --> 00:04:54.560
What has happened
to our country?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.696
-Come on, now, what about
when he said that

00:04:56.696 --> 00:05:01.567
Hillary should be locked up,
or bullied Greta Thunberg?

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.703
That didn't change your mind?

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:07.306
-He didn't do those things,
though.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.175
-Yes, he did.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.844
-But then he said he didn't,

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.446
so, you know, who's to say?

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:15.848
-All right, look.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.617
So you've totally changed
your mind based on this,

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:20.953
based on a gift basket?

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.255
-Not completely.

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.089
We still have to hear
from the experts,

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:25.991
the basket manufacturer.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:28.694
The fish.
Martha Stewart, probably.

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:30.463
-Yeah, I -- I don't think
that they --

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.465
-I mean, what does the
<i> sturgeon</i> general think?

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.400
-No, no, no.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.769
-Look, Jimmy, there's a legal
precedent for shading someone

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.304
by taking their fish eggs.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.105
The Supreme Court ruled on it.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:42.041
-In what case?

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.943
-Roe v Shade.
-Roe v Shade.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.344
-Yeah, okay, that's enough.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:48.147
The one guy who changed
his mind on Trump, everybody.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.316
I guess Biden just got
another vote.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.451
-Actually, I'm voting
for Kanye. Whoo!

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:54.554
-Please, please, please,
get it -- please.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:56.556
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.191
[ Sighs ]

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.659
Meanwhile, as the president
is dealing with his relatives,

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.695
the coronavirus rages on.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:06.299
In response to a spike in cases,
California governor Gavin Newsom

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.300
has had to make some
tough decisions.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.670 line:0%
-This morning, as California
sees a surge

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:13.473 line:0%
in coronavirus cases,
the nation's largest state

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.574 line:0%
rolling back its reopening.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:18.877 line:0%
Governor Gavin Newsom ordering
the closure of in-door dining,

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:23.049 line:0%
bars, movie theaters, and even
zoos across the state.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.051
-There's actually a name
for staying home

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.885
and wearing a mask
in California.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:29.054
It's called getting a nose job.

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:32.224
[ Laughter ]
-Ohh!

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:33.692
Oh, oh!

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:36.328
-[ Chuckling ] Oh!
-Ha, ha.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:37.863
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:42.034
There. Me?

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:43.302
-Went there.
-Yeah.

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:44.970
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:48.507
That's right.
Bars and zoos are also closed.

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:50.343
It's a real bummer if your
favorite activity

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.945
is to get drunk and then
go yell at some penguins.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:58.251
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:00.052
Can I --
Can I come back to --

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.887
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:04.990
Can I come back to here?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.159
New York has decided
to be extra careful,

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.895
but others are going in
a slightly different direction.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.597
Check out what just reopened.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:13.399 line:0%
-Disney World's welcoming
guests back

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:17.136 line:0%
at their Magic Kingdom
and Animal Kingdom parks.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:19.705
-It's crazy. Right now
the boring part of Disney

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.907
is the roller coaster,
while the scariest part

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:23.742
is standing in line.

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:26.445
You know Disney's being reckless
because the character

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:28.681
greeting everyone at the front
gate is Sneezy.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.916
I think -- Why --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:33.819
There's six other choices.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:35.221
Yeah, the park is open,

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:36.989
but if you fail
the temperature check,

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:38.490
you get locked inside
"It's a Small World"

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.758
for two weeks.

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:42.428
And that can -- that can do
some serious D.

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:46.432
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.601
But this --

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.269
I heard it somewhere,
you can say --

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.772
-No, you did not --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:55.841
I could do some serious D, man.
-No. No.

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:57.943
-Mess you up a little bit.
-No!

00:07:57.943 --> 00:08:00.379
Mess you up a little bit.
-Stop it.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.015
-Oh, this is nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.184
This is nice, though.
For $20, they will sell you

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:07.820
a picture of the exact moment
that you get the virus.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.055
Isn't that cool?

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.323
Maybe I'm being too
tough, though.

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:12.724
Disney is doing
the best they can.

00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:14.960
For instance, the two guys
inside the Pluto costume

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.230
are now facing
opposite ways.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:21.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.969
Disney World has decided
to reopen,

00:08:23.969 --> 00:08:26.538
while other places are being
a little more cautious.

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:29.207 line:0%
-KFC is reportedly
shutting dining rooms

00:08:29.207 --> 00:08:32.010 line:0%
at its company-owned restaurants
in Florida.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:35.381 line:0%
The company has also told
franchise owners to consider

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:37.950 line:0%
doing the same in COVID-19
hot spots,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.987 line:0%
including Arizona, California,
Florida, and Texas.

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:45.024
-Yeah, KFC wants everyone
to stay healthy...

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:46.591
while they eat a bucket
of fried chicken

00:08:46.591 --> 00:08:48.794
and big gulp of gravy.

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.997
KFC is actually a good choice
during the pandemic

00:08:50.997 --> 00:08:52.765
because when you're done
with your meal,

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:55.067
you can turn your empty bucket
into a face shield.

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.869
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.737
And it's not just KFC
that's taking precautions.

00:08:58.737 --> 00:09:01.007
Today White Castle
announced...

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:03.276
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:05.311
Dude, this is for real.
This is serious.

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:07.913
White Castle announced that it
plans to test a cooking robot

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:09.648
named Flippy.
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:11.651
-Wait, what?

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:14.186
-They invented a robot
named Flippy,

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:16.922
and in at least one
of its kitchens this fall

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:18.324
they're gonna unveil it.

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:19.792
This is real.
Take a look at Flippy.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:23.429
♪♪

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.397
[ Laughter ]
-That's --

00:09:25.397 --> 00:09:27.599
-Dude, that is the last thing
you want to see

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:29.035
when you're stoned and going
to White Castle,

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:32.004
a robot arm wearing a shirt,
flipping burgers.

00:09:32.004 --> 00:09:34.172
"What?!"

00:09:34.172 --> 00:09:36.175
After one shift,
Flippy was like,

00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:37.876
[ Robot voice ] "I should have
stayed in school.

00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:40.546
My brother is an MRI machine."

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:42.047
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:44.050
And finally, everybody,
our country is still

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.584
in the middle of a pandemic.

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.686
And yesterday, Education
Secretary Betsy De Vos

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:49.555
defended the administration's
push

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:51.590
to reopen schools this fall.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.392
Even though many parents
disagree,

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:57.062
some think it's possible
if kids wear masks.

00:09:57.062 --> 00:10:00.266
It's a complicated situation,
so we have PTA president

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:04.703 line:0%
and mom of four, Deb Brown
here to help break it down.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:06.372 line:0%
Deb?

00:10:06.372 --> 00:10:08.507 line:0%
-Oh, hi, hi, Jimmy,
you actually caught us

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:11.310 line:0%
during a brief park break.
-That's great.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.178
Well, why don't you tell us
little bit about why

00:10:13.178 --> 00:10:15.781
you think kids should go back
to school?

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.550
-Hmm. Well, Jimmy,
it's simple --

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.852
masks work for us, and they'll
work for our kids.

00:10:20.852 --> 00:10:23.422
I mean, they really --
Hey, kiddos.

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:27.325
Masks on, okay?
What did we talk about? Hmm?

00:10:27.325 --> 00:10:28.793
We just really really need
to teach them

00:10:28.793 --> 00:10:30.663
that it's our new normal.

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:32.530
-But don't you think that
it will be difficult

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:35.701
for teachers to navigate on top
of everything else?

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:39.838
-I mean, 7th grade algebra is
hard to navigate, Jimmy.

00:10:39.838 --> 00:10:41.273
This is something teachers --

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:42.808
Honey, it goes around your nose
and your mouth,

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:44.376
not your nose and your eyes.

00:10:44.376 --> 00:10:45.711
You don't breathe
with your eyes.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:48.246
Use your brain, think.
-Oh, my God.

00:10:48.246 --> 00:10:50.082
-That teachers won't
have to worry about

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:52.151
because it will be natural.

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:55.187
-Yeah, but some people think
it might be distracting.

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:56.655
-Distracting?

00:10:56.655 --> 00:10:59.725
Jimmy, we've got cellphones,
iPads, SMART Boards.

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:03.228
Johnny, if you snap his elastic
one more time, no TV,

00:11:03.228 --> 00:11:05.598
and I swear to God,
this time I will do it.

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:10.102
It won't be any more
distracting.

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:12.270
-SMART Boards.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.706
But you don't think we're making
a hard situation

00:11:14.706 --> 00:11:16.575
even more difficult?

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:19.344
-I mean, I think it's already
hard for all of us.

00:11:19.344 --> 00:11:21.180
And how are they both wet?

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:23.849
How are the brand new masks
I just gave you both

00:11:23.849 --> 00:11:27.653
absolutely
sopping wet, huh?

00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:29.822
I mean, we all have to be
flexible.

00:11:29.822 --> 00:11:33.826
-Do you think it's something
kids will even be able to do?

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:38.463
-Jimmy.
Jimmy, our kids can do anything.

00:11:38.463 --> 00:11:39.764
You can't paint it!

00:11:39.764 --> 00:11:41.767
Well, if you paint it,
then you can't breathe!

00:11:41.767 --> 00:11:43.168
That defeats the purpose
of the mask!

00:11:43.168 --> 00:11:44.670
Give me the -- Come on,
give me the paint brush.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.205
No, do not put the paint brush
in your mouth.

00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:48.740
You take it out.
No, stop painting your brother!

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:52.043
Do not paint him!
Do not paint him!

00:11:52.043 --> 00:11:54.947
-Wow. Wow.

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:56.182
-[ Clears throat ]

00:11:58.083 --> 00:12:00.519
Our kids can do anything
they put their minds to.

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:02.855
-Okay, sure. But...

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:04.857
-Hey, get the --

00:12:04.857 --> 00:12:06.091
[ Laughter ]

00:12:06.091 --> 00:12:08.260
...way too fast!
-Okay, hey --

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.161
-If Jason puts the bugs
in his own mask --

00:12:10.161 --> 00:12:12.330
-Okay. Sorry --
-...then stop!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.400
-Is this a bad time?
If this is a bad time --

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:17.269
-Stop feeding the bugs
to your brother, Johnny.

00:12:17.269 --> 00:12:18.536
-Okay --

00:12:18.536 --> 00:12:20.806
PTA president Deb Brown,
everybody.

00:12:20.806 --> 00:12:22.575
We have a great show
for you tonight.

